CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1785287886
OL,3,CFourth heatwave of year to peak with
OL,4,Ctemperatures of up to 35C
OL,6,FIt comes as Royal Parks staff were
OL,7,Fadvised not to leave deckchairs under
OL,8,Ftrees over fears branches will fall
OL,9,Fduring hot weather.
OL,11,FLarge-scale wildfires across Europe,
OL,12,Fincluding in parts of Spain, France
OL,13,Fand Greece, have led to evacuations,
OL,14,Fenvironmental damage and pressure on
OL,15,Fthe emergency services.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30407
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1785287886
OL,3,CFourth heatwave of year to peak with
OL,4,Ctemperatures of up to 35C
OL,6,FThe NFCC said UK wildfires are
OL,7,Ftypically smaller and different in
OL,8,Fnature to those seen in southern
OL,9,FEurope, adding, however, that the
OL,10,F"long-term effects of climate change
OL,11,Fare increasing the likelihood of
OL,12,Flarger, more complex and more resource-
OL,13,Fintensive wildfire incidents
OL,14,Foccurring".
OL,16,FPhil Garrigan, chairman of the NFCC,
OL,17,Fsaid: "More than 200 wildfires in just
OL,18,F12 days shows how quickly the risk can
OL,19,Fescalate when hot, dry conditions take
OL,20,Fhold.
OL,26,@rD@AOUvD@JO]yD@GOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30408
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1785287886
OL,3,CFourth heatwave of year to peak with
OL,4,Ctemperatures of up to 35C
OL,6,F"The scenes we're seeing across parts
OL,7,Fof Europe are a stark reminder of what
OL,8,Fa changing climate means for fire and
OL,9,Frescue services.
OL,11,F"We are not seeing fires of that scale
OL,12,Fin the UK today, but the science tells
OL,13,Fus we should expect larger, more
OL,14,Ffrequent and more complex wildfires in
OL,15,Fthe future.
OL,17,F"That's why we need continued
OL,18,Finvestment in specialist wildfire
OL,19,Fcapabilities, including aerial
OL,20,Ffirefighting support, so we're
OL,21,Fprepared for the risks ahead.
OL,26,@nD@AOUsD@AOUyD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30409
SC,0009
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1785287886
OL,3,CFourth heatwave of year to peak with
OL,4,Ctemperatures of up to 35C
OL,6,F"But prevention remains our strongest
OL,7,Fdefence. Most wildfires are avoidable,
OL,8,Fand we're asking everyone to take
OL,9,Fextra care during the hot weather to
OL,10,Fhelp keep their communities safe."
OL,12,FA Ministry of Housing, Communities &
OL,13,FLocal Government spokesperson said:
OL,14,F"We're investing nearly #100 million
OL,15,Fto help replace assets which can be
OL,16,Fused to tackle wildfires, including
OL,17,Fdedicated off-road vehicles which are
OL,18,Fsuitable for England's landscape.
OL,26,@nD@AOUrD@bO]vD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G9/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30410
SC,0010
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1785287886
OL,3,CFourth heatwave of year to peak with
OL,4,Ctemperatures of up to 35C
OL,6,F"This includes rolling out a pilot to
OL,7,Fplace highly trained firefighters who
OL,8,Fspecialise in wildfire response in key
OL,9,Flocations across England, working with
OL,10,Findustry experts to ensure this
OL,11,Fapproach is tailored to the unique
OL,12,Fwildfire risks here."
OL,14,FFire chiefs said many wildfires are
OL,15,Fcaused by everyday human activity,
OL,16,Fadding that "disposing of cigarettes
OL,17,Fsafely, avoiding the use of disposable
OL,18,Fbarbecues in open spaces and taking
OL,19,Flitter home can significantly reduce
OL,20,Fthe risk of fires starting".
OL,26,@nD@AOUtD@UO]xD@MOU|D@[O]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G10/11
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30411
SC,0011
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1785287886
OL,3,CFourth heatwave of year to peak with
OL,4,Ctemperatures of up to 35C
OL,6,FJuly has been 3C above average across
OL,7,Fthe UK, according to provisional Met
OL,8,FOffice data, potentially putting it
OL,9,Famong the hottest three or four months
OL,10,Fof July on record.
OL,12,FFire chiefs said people should report
OL,13,Fany signs of fire immediately by
OL,14,Fcalling 999 and asking for the fire
OL,15,Fand rescue service.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                   G11/11
